        p([r("This is the most important step and most people skip it. Before TJ contacts any PE firm, he should spend 15 minutes on their website and LinkedIn. Know:",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        bul("Which portfolio companies are manufacturers with CNC or fabrication equipment"),
        bul("Which portfolio companies were acquired in the last 12\u201318 months (they are most likely still assessing and improving operations)"),
        bul("Whether the firm has announced any add-on acquisitions (active deal activity = active diligence needs)"),
        bul("Who specifically on the deal team covers industrial / manufacturing deals \u2014 target that person, not the firm\u2019s main line"),
        sp(60),
        p([r("TJ\u2019s goal is to walk into every conversation sounding like someone who has done his homework \u2014 not someone reading from a script. \u2018I noticed your firm recently acquired [Portfolio Company], which appears to be a precision machining operation\u2019 opens every door.",{size:19,color:DARK,italics:true})]),
      ],NAVY),

      sp(40),

      stepBox("2","MAKE FIRST CONTACT BY EMAIL OR LINKEDIN \u2014 Not Phone",[
        p([r("PE professionals receive phone calls from service vendors constantly and screen most of them. A well-crafted, specific email or LinkedIn message stands out because it shows TJ did his homework. Phone follow-up comes after the written introduction.",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        bul("Email is preferred for senior contacts (Partners, MDs, Operating Partners). Find emails using Hunter.io, Apollo.io, or the firm\u2019s website contact page."),
        bul("LinkedIn messages are effective for Associates, VPs, and Principals who are active on the platform"),
        bul("Subject line for email: \u2018Equipment Expertise for Your Manufacturing Portfolio \u2014 [Firm Name]\u2019 or \u2018Equipment Valuation for [Recent Acquisition Name]\u2019"),
        bul("Keep the message to 4\u20135 sentences: who TJ is, what specific expertise he has, one relevant fact about their portfolio, and one low-friction offer (a sample report or a 15-minute call)"),
        sp(60),
        p([r("One week after the email, follow up by phone. This is now a warm call, not cold outreach.",{size:19,color:DARK,bold:true})]),
      ],PURPLE),

      sp(40),

      stepBox("3","POSITION TJ AS A DEAL RESOURCE, NOT A VENDOR",[
        p([r("This is the framing that separates TJ from every other equipment dealer they\u2019ve heard from. He is not selling a service \u2014 he is offering deal-critical intelligence that directly affects their purchase price, their debt structure, and their value creation plan.",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        bul("Use language that resonates with PE professionals: \u2018acquisition diligence,\u2019 \u2018collateral value,\u2019 \u2018capex planning,\u2019 \u2018value creation,\u2019 \u2018balance sheet asset\u2019"),
        bul("Lead with the financial impact: \u2018Equipment is often 30\u201360% of a manufacturing company\u2019s total asset value. Getting that number wrong in diligence affects the purchase price, the debt structure, and the return model.\u2019"),
        bul("Reference TJ\u2019s 25+ years of active market experience as differentiated expertise, not just tenure \u2014 \u2018I am an active buyer and seller of this equipment, not a desk-based generalist appraiser\u2019"),
        bul("Offer a specific, fast deliverable: \u201848-hour equipment valuation from the time you send me the machine list\u2019"),
      ],TEAL),

      sp(40),

      stepBox("4","OFFER THE DUE DILIGENCE REPORT AS THE DOOR-OPENER",[
        p([r("The most effective first engagement for PE is a complimentary diligence-phase equipment valuation on a deal they are currently considering. This is a higher-stakes version of the free report tactic used with banks, and it works even better because the financial consequences are larger.",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        p([r("The offer:",{bold:true,size:19,color:GREEN})]),
        bul("\u2018If you have an industrial company in your diligence pipeline right now, I\u2019d be glad to provide a complimentary equipment valuation to give you a preview of our reporting quality and turnaround time. You compare it to whatever you\u2019re currently using and make your own call.\u2019"),
        sp(40),
        p([r("Why this works:",{bold:true,size:19,color:GREEN})]),
        bul("PE firms are always working on deals \u2014 there is almost always something in the pipeline"),
        bul("The free report eliminates all risk on their side"),
        bul("A 48-hour turnaround on a thorough equipment valuation will immediately distinguish TJ from every generalist appraiser they have used before"),
        bul("Once TJ\u2019s report is in the data room, he is the established expert for that deal \u2014 and for the portfolio company ongoing"),
      ],GREEN),

      sp(40),

      stepBox("5","CONVERT THE DEAL RELATIONSHIP TO A PORTFOLIO RELATIONSHIP",[
        p([r("The deal closes. TJ has been involved in the diligence. Now the real opportunity begins: the portfolio company is under active PE ownership and will need equipment support for years. This is TJ\u2019s moment to make the transition from deal resource to trusted ongoing advisor.",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        bul("After the deal closes, reach out to both the PE deal team and the portfolio company\u2019s CEO or COO: \u2018Congratulations on the close. I\u2019d love to continue as your go-to resource for equipment valuation, sourcing, and advisory at [Portfolio Company].\u2019"),
        bul("Offer a post-acquisition equipment review: a full inventory and valuation of every machine on the floor, formatted as a balance sheet asset schedule. This is typically the first thing a PE operations team needs after close."),
        bul("Ask the deal team: \u2018Do you have other portfolio companies in manufacturing where this kind of equipment expertise would be useful? I\u2019m happy to extend the same service.\u2019"),
        bul("This single conversation can turn one deal into five ongoing relationships across a firm\u2019s entire manufacturing portfolio."),
      ],GOLD),

      sp(40),

      stepBox("6","ATTEND ACG EVENTS AND BUILD IN-PERSON RELATIONSHIPS",[
        p([r("No email, LinkedIn message, or cold call is as effective as meeting someone in person at an industry event. ACG Nashville and ACG Kentucky are the premier gathering places for the exact people TJ is targeting. He should be at every event.",{size:19,color:DARK})],{spacing:{before:0,after:60}}),
        bul("ACG Nashville holds monthly networking events, deal forums, and an annual awards gala. Attendance at each event is typically $75\u2013$150 for non-members."),
        bul("At every event, TJ\u2019s introduction is: \u2018I\u2019m TJ Opincar with Opincar Machinery \u2014 we specialize in heavy CNC machinery. I work with PE firms doing due diligence on manufacturing acquisitions. 25 years in this market.\u2019 That\u2019s it. Short, specific, memorable."),
        bul("Bring business cards and the one-page capability sheet to every event. The sample valuation report as a PDF on the phone if someone asks to see an example."),
        bul("Follow up within 24 hours of meeting someone meaningful: a brief LinkedIn connection with a note referencing the conversation."),
      ],STEEL),

      sp(120),

      // ── PART 6: SCRIPTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
      divider(),
      sectionHeader("PART 6:  WORD-FOR-WORD SCRIPTS FOR PE OUTREACH"),
      sp(80),

      p([r("Cold Email to a PE Deal Team Member \u2014 Right After an Acquisition Announcement",{bold:true,size:21,color:NAVY})]),
      sp(40),
      scriptBox("Subject: Equipment Expertise for [Portfolio Company Name] \u2014 Opincar Machinery",
        "\u201CHi [Name],\n\nI saw that [PE Firm] recently closed on [Portfolio Company] \u2014 congratulations. I\u2019m TJ Opincar with Opincar Machinery in Smyrna, Tennessee. I\u2019ve spent 25+ years as an active buyer and seller of heavy CNC machinery \u2014 boring mills, machining centers, lathes, grinders, and fabrication equipment.\n\nI work with PE firms during and after manufacturing acquisitions to provide fast, accurate equipment valuations for the acquisition model, ongoing portfolio support, and capex advisory. Our standard turnaround is 48 hours.\n\nIf it would be useful, I\u2019d be glad to send a sample valuation report so you can see our format, or to provide a complimentary equipment assessment on [Portfolio Company]\u2019s shop floor as you work through your post-acquisition plan.\n\nEither way, happy to be a resource. Would a brief call make sense?\n\nTJ Opincar\u201D"
      ),

      sp(80),

      p([r("LinkedIn Message to a VP at an Industrial PE Firm",{bold:true,size:21,color:NAVY})]),
      sp(40),
      scriptBox("Keep it short \u2014 the goal is a reply, not a pitch:",
        "\u201CHi [Name] \u2014 I noticed [PE Firm] focuses on industrial and manufacturing investments. I\u2019m TJ Opincar with Opincar Machinery \u2014 25+ years in heavy CNC machinery as an active buyer and seller. I work with PE deal teams on equipment valuations during manufacturing acquisitions \u2014 48-hour turnaround. Happy to send a sample report if that\u2019s useful. No pressure.\u201D"
      ),

      sp(80),

      p([r("Phone Follow-Up Script \u2014 After Email Was Sent",{bold:true,size:21,color:NAVY})]),
      sp(40),
      scriptBox("When you reach them live:",
        "\u201CHi [Name], this is TJ Opincar with Opincar Machinery. I sent you an email last week about our equipment valuation service for PE-backed manufacturers. I\u2019ll be brief \u2014 I\u2019ve been in heavy CNC machinery for 25 years, buying and selling boring mills, machining centers, lathes and fabrication equipment across the Southeast. I work with PE firms during diligence and after close to give them an accurate, fast FMV on the machinery in their portfolio. 48-hour turnaround, and I know these machines because I\u2019ve personally bought and sold them \u2014 I\u2019m not reading a price guide.\n\nDo you have a manufacturing acquisition in your pipeline right now where an equipment valuation would be useful? Or a portfolio company where you\u2019d like a current asset value?\u201D"
      ),

      sp(80),

      p([r("Handling \u2018We Already Have Appraisers We Use\u2019",{bold:true,size:21,color:NAVY})]),
      sp(40),
      scriptBox("The most common PE objection \u2014 here is TJ\u2019s answer:",
        "\u201CThat makes sense \u2014 most firms do. What I\u2019d offer is a faster option for when speed matters on a live deal, and deeper expertise on CNC and fabrication equipment specifically. Most appraisers are generalists. I\u2019m an active market participant \u2014 I\u2019ve personally bought and sold boring mills, machining centers, and lathes for 25 years, and I know what buyers are actually paying right now, not what a guide says. If you ever have a deal where industrial machinery is the core asset, I\u2019d appreciate the chance to show you one report. Then you decide.\u201D"
      ),

      sp(80),

      p([r("At an ACG Event \u2014 In-Person Introduction",{bold:true,size:21,color:NAVY})]),
      sp(40),
      scriptBox("When asked what TJ does \u2014 30 seconds, no jargon:",
        "\u201CI run Opincar Machinery in Smyrna \u2014 we buy and sell heavy industrial CNC equipment. I also work with PE firms doing due diligence on manufacturing acquisitions. If a company has boring mills, machining centers, lathes, or fabrication equipment on the shop floor, I can tell you exactly what it\u2019s worth and what condition it\u2019s actually in \u2014 in 48 hours. 25 years doing this. Who\u2019s your firm?\u201D"
      ),

      sp(120),

      // ── PART 7: WEEKLY RHYTHM ────────────────────────────────────────────
      divider(),
      sectionHeader("PART 7:  TJ\u2019S WEEKLY PE PROSPECTING RHYTHM"),
      sp(80),

      p([r("PE prospecting is slower and more relationship-intensive than bank prospecting. The volume is lower but the deal size is larger. TJ should spend 3\u20134 hours per week on PE-specific outreach, running parallel to his bank lender activity.",{size:20,color:DARK,bold:true})]),
      sp(80),

      new Table({
        width:{size:9360,type:WidthType.DXA},columnWidths:[1800,7560],
        rows:[
          new TableRow({children:[
            new TableCell({shading:{fill:NAVY,type:ShadingType.CLEAR},borders:none,margins:{top:80,bottom:80,left:160,right:160},width:{size:1800,type:WidthType.DXA},children:[p([r("WHEN",{bold:true,size:18,color:WHITE})],{alignment:AlignmentType.CENTER})]}),
            new TableCell({shading:{fill:NAVY,type:ShadingType.CLEAR},borders:none,margins:{top:80,bottom:80,left:160,right:160},width:{size:7560,type:WidthType.DXA},children:[p([r("WHAT TJ DOES",{bold:true,size:18,color:WHITE})])]}),
          ]}),
          ...[
            ["Monday\n(30 min)","Check Google Alerts and LinkedIn for any manufacturing acquisition announcements from PE firms on TJ\u2019s target list. If a deal closed in the last 72 hours, that firm jumps to the top of the outreach queue. Research the portfolio company before reaching out."],
            ["Tuesday\n(45 min)","Send 3\u20135 outreach emails or LinkedIn messages to PE contacts. Each one is personalized and references a specific portfolio company, recent deal, or investment thesis relevant to TJ\u2019s expertise. No mass messages."],
            ["Wednesday\n(30 min)","Phone follow-up on any email sent 5\u20137 days ago that has not received a reply. Leave voicemail if no answer. Log all activity in the prospect spreadsheet."],
            ["Thursday\n(30 min)","Research 3 new PE firms or M&A advisors for the prospect list. Visit their websites, review portfolio companies, identify the right deal team contact on LinkedIn. Add to the spreadsheet."],
            ["Friday\n(15 min)","Review the week. Update the prospect spreadsheet with contact status and next action. Identify the top priority follow-ups for the coming week."],
            ["Monthly\n(ACG Event)","Attend one ACG Nashville or ACG Kentucky event. Bring business cards and the one-page capability sheet. Follow up within 24 hours with every meaningful contact made at the event."],
            ["Quarterly\n(60 min)","Review all active PE relationships. Reach out to every PE contact who has used TJ in the past with a brief market update: 3\u20135 bullet points on used CNC machinery pricing trends, demand levels, and any notable auction results. Keeps TJ visible and adds value without being transactional."],
          ].map(([when,what],i) => new TableRow({children:[
            new TableCell({shading:{fill:i%2===0?LT_BLUE:WHITE,type:ShadingType.CLEAR},borders:tb(),margins:{top:100,bottom:100,left:140,right:140},width:{size:1800,type:WidthType.DXA},children:[p([r(when,{bold:true,size:18,color:NAVY})],{alignment:AlignmentType.CENTER})]}),
            new TableCell({shading:{fill:i%2===0?LT_BLUE:WHITE,type:ShadingType.CLEAR},borders:tb(),margins:{top:100,bottom:100,left:140,right:140},width:{size:7560,type:WidthType.DXA},children:[p([r(what,{size:19,color:DARK})])]}),
          ]}))
        ]
      }),

      sp(80),

      box([
        p([r("REALISTIC EXPECTATIONS FOR PE OUTREACH",{bold:true,size:20,color:NAVY})]),
        sp(60),
        p([r("PE relationships take longer to establish than bank relationships but generate significantly larger individual engagements. A single pre-acquisition equipment diligence engagement for a PE firm can be worth $5,000\u2013$25,000. One trusted GP relationship at a firm like LFM Capital or MiddleGround, where they are actively acquiring manufacturers, can generate $50,000\u2013$150,000 per year in ongoing valuation, advisory, and sourcing work across their portfolio.",{size:19,color:DARK})]),
        sp(60),
        p([r("Month 1\u20133: Build the research list, make 15\u201325 initial contacts, attend 2\u20133 ACG events. Goal: 2\u20133 conversations with qualified prospects.",{size:19,color:DARK,bold:true})]),
        p([r("Month 3\u20136: First 1\u20133 paid engagements. Referrals begin from deal teams and M&A advisors. Goal: establish 2\u20133 PE relationships.",{size:19,color:DARK,bold:true})],{spacing:{before:40}}),
        p([r("Month 6\u201312: Compounding relationships. Each PE firm with multiple portfolio companies generates recurring work. Goal: 3\u20135 PE firms treating TJ as their default industrial equipment resource.",{size:19,color:DARK,bold:true})],{spacing:{before:40}}),
      ],LT_GOLD,{top:sb(GOLD,4),bottom:sb(GOLD,4),left:sb(GOLD,4),right:sb(GOLD,4)},{top:160,bottom:160,left:240,right:240}),

      sp(120),

      // ── CLOSE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      box([
        p([r("Private equity firms are making multi-million dollar bets on manufacturing businesses.",{bold:true,size:24,color:WHITE})],{alignment:AlignmentType.CENTER}),
        sp(80),
        p([r("The value of those bets depends heavily on what the equipment on the shop floor is actually worth \u2014 not what a generalist appraiser estimated from a desk, but what an active market participant with 25 years of firsthand experience says it\u2019s worth. That person is TJ Opincar. The PE firms who work with him get better diligence, faster turnarounds, and a trusted advisor who understands exactly what those machines do and what they sell for in today\u2019s market. The ones who don\u2019t are guessing.",{size:20,color:"AAC8E8"})],{alignment:AlignmentType.CENTER}),
        sp(80),
        p([r("TJ Opincar  \u00B7  Opincar Machinery  \u00B7  Smyrna, TN  \u00B7  (615) 459-7983  \u00B7  tom@opincarmachinery.com  \u00B7  opincarmachinery.com",{size:18,color:"7FA8C9"})],{alignment:AlignmentType.CENTER}),
      ],NAVY,none,{top:240,bottom:240,left:360,right:360}),
    ]
  }]
});

Packer.toBuffer(doc).then(buf => {
  fs.writeFileSync('/home/claude/pe_acquisition_guide.docx', buf);
  console.log('Done!');
});

